<DocsLayout title="Independent capabilities in Haft v9" description="The former five-modes page now explains why v9 skills are independent capabilities rather than a project workflow.">
  <h1>Independent capabilities</h1>

  <div class="callout-warn">
    <p>
      <strong>The five-mode workflow is not the v9 contract.</strong> This URL is
      retained so old links reach the correction instead of teaching a removed
      product model.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    v9 does not require
    <code>Understand → Explore → Choose → Execute → Verify</code>. Skills are
    independent <code>MethodDescription</code> carriers with their own entry
    conditions and result boundaries. Completion of one skill does not make the
    next skill mandatory.
  </p>

  <h2>Select by the current condition</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Condition</th>
        <th>Capability</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>The question is ambiguous and FPF pattern choice may matter</td><td><code>h-reason</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The problem is under-articulated</td><td><code>h-frame</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>A concrete failure has rival explanations</td><td><code>h-diagnose</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Distinct approaches are needed</td><td><code>h-explore</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Existing candidates need fair comparison</td><td><code>h-compare</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The operator directly binds one exact choice</td><td><code>h-decide</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>A recorded claim must be checked against reality</td><td><code>h-verify</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Project state or readiness is the question</td><td><code>h-status</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Setup or project profile is incomplete</td><td><code>h-onboard</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>A typed specification or lifecycle act is current</td><td><code>h-spec</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The operator asks to save one non-binding observation</td><td><code>h-note</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The operator grants bounded execution authority</td><td><code>h-commission</code> (manual only)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Ordered work still exists</h2>

  <p>
    Removing a universal skill sequence does not make FPF acausal or forbid
    planning. An explicit causal claim, ordered <code>MethodDescription</code>,
    <code>WorkPlan</code>, or performed-work relation may carry order when that
    order is current. It is not inferred from a documentation page, skill list,
    or graph layout.
  </p>

  <h2>Persistence and authority</h2>

  <p>
    Most bounded reasoning may stay in conversation. Durable records are
    created only for an explicit save/bind request or a concrete receiving use.
    A plan is not performed work, a recommendation is not a decision, and a
    DecisionRecord is not a WorkCommission.
  </p>

